IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc17-sor.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 490.011 to 490.019: sex offender information: the definitions (with the tables of primary and secondary offences), the order to comply
-- with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, its duration, reasons, appeal, termination, notice, and the obligation of a person served with a notice in Form 53. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Same conventions as ccc17-dna-orders.l4. The designated offence is the module's own `s 490.011(1) ...` answer (rule R3: a different function from `s 487.04 designated offence`). Seam OUT (ccc18 asks):
-- `s 490.012 an order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act is in force` (MAYBE BOOLEAN), and the functions `s 490.011(1) designated offence` and `s 490.019 ...`.

§ `Section 490.011 -- Interpretation: definitions`

DECLARE `s 490.011(1) enactment` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.011(1) this Act`
    `s 490.011(1) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983`
    `s 490.011(1) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83`
    `s 490.011(1) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988`
    `s 490.011(1) this Act, as it read from time to time before December 6, 2014`

DECLARE `s 490.011(1) offence` HAS
    `enactment`                                                        IS A `s 490.011(1) enactment`
    `provision`                                                        IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `it is an attempt or conspiracy to commit that offence`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the intent is to commit an offence referred to in any of subparagraphs (b)(i) to (iv)`   IS A BOOLEAN

