-- "primary offence means" (a) to (e) and (f): an attempt or conspiracy to commit an offence referred to in (a) to (e). The offence is identified by its enactment and provision; for an attempt or conspiracy
-- they identify the offence attempted. A closed definition: an offence outside the six limbs is JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 490.011(1) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.011(1) primary offence` MEANS
    IF `s 490.011(1) the offence is one referred to in paragraphs (a) to (e) of the definition of primary offence` `the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "primary offence means"

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 490.011(1) offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 490.011(1) the offence is one referred to in paragraphs (a) to (e) of the definition of primary offence` MEANS
        (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 490.011(1) this Act` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 490.011(1) primary offence (a) the provisions`)
    OR  (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 490.011(1) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 490.011(1) primary offence (b) the provisions` AND ((`the offence`'s `provision`) EQUALS (`Provision of the Code` OF 246, "(1)") IMPLIES `the offence`'s `the intent is to commit an offence referred to in any of subparagraphs (b)(i) to (iv)`))
    OR  (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 490.011(1) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 490.011(1) primary offence (c) the provisions`)
    OR  (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 490.011(1) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 490.011(1) primary offence (d) the provisions`)
    OR  (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 490.011(1) this Act, as it read from time to time before December 6, 2014` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 490.011(1) primary offence (e) the provisions`)

