-- covers: 490.011(1) "designated offence"
-- jural: none
-- src:10063 | designated offence means a primary offence or a secondary offence. (infraction désignée)
@ref s 490.011(1) "designated offence" (src:10063)
-- "designated offence means a primary offence or a secondary offence". A caller (ccc18) asks this by name: the answer is the offence's own.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 490.011(1) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.011(1) designated offence` MEANS
    IF `s 490.011(1) primary offence` `the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 490.011(1) secondary offence` `the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "designated offence means a primary offence or a secondary offence"

-- covers: 490.011(1), 490.011(1) "crime of a sexual nature"
