GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.011(1) verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` MEANS
    IF `it is a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder within the meaning of subsection 672.1(1)` OR `it is a finding of not responsible on account of mental disorder within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder means a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder within the meaning of subsection 672.1(1)"

-- covers: 490.011(2), 490.011(2)(a), 490.011(2)(b)
-- jural: a young person > the court > immunity
-- src:10150 | (2) For the purpose of this section and sections 490.012 to 490.032, a person who is convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, a designated offence does not include a young person
-- src:10151 | (a) within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act unless they are given an adult sentence within the meaning of that subsection for the offence; or
-- src:10152 | (b) within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, unless they are convicted of the offence in ordinary court within the meaning of that subsection.
@ref s 490.011(2) (src:10150-10152)
-- A person convicted of, or found not criminally responsible for, a designated offence "does not include a young person" (a) under the Youth Criminal Justice Act unless given an adult sentence; (b) under the Young
-- Offenders Act unless convicted in ordinary court. The subsection only excludes: for anyone else it says nothing (NOTHING).
GIVEN `the person is a young person within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is given an adult sentence within the meaning of that subsection for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a young person within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted of the offence in ordinary court within the meaning of that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.011(2) the person is not included among those convicted of, or found not criminally responsible for, a designated offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a young person within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` AND `the person is given an adult sentence within the meaning of that subsection for the offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they are given an adult sentence within the meaning of that subsection for the offence"
        IF `the person is a young person within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a young person within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act` AND `the person is convicted of the offence in ordinary court within the meaning of that subsection` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they are convicted of the offence in ordinary court within the meaning of that subsection"
        IF `the person is a young person within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§ `Section 490.012 -- Order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`

-- covers: 490.012(5)
-- jural: a person convicted of a secondary offence > the court > immunity
-- src:10178 | (5) A court shall make an order under any of subsections (1) to (3) in respect of a secondary offence only if the prosecutor applies for the order and establishes beyond a reasonable doubt that the person committed the secondary offence with the intent to commit a primary offence.
@ref s 490.012(5) (src:10178)
-- "A court shall make an order under any of subsections (1) to (3) in respect of a secondary offence only if the prosecutor applies ... and establishes beyond a reasonable doubt that the person committed the
-- secondary offence with the intent to commit a primary offence": closed with "only if" (JUST FALSE when it fails). For an offence that is not a secondary offence the limitation says nothing (NOTHING).
GIVEN `s 490.011(1) secondary offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor applies for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor establishes beyond a reasonable doubt that the person committed the secondary offence with the intent to commit a primary offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.012(5) the court may make an order in respect of the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 490.011(1) secondary offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the prosecutor applies for the order` AND `the prosecutor establishes beyond a reasonable doubt that the person committed the secondary offence with the intent to commit a primary offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if the prosecutor applies for the order and establishes beyond a reasonable doubt that the person committed the secondary offence with the intent to commit a primary offence"

-- covers: 490.012(1), 490.012(1)(a), 490.012(1)(b), 490.012(1)(c)
-- fork: F11
-- jural: a person sentenced for a designated offence > the court > liability
-- src:10156 | 490.012 (1) Subject to subsection (5), when a court imposes a sentence on a person for a designated offence, it shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act if
-- src:10157 | (a) the designated offence was prosecuted by indictment;
-- src:10158 | (b) the sentence for the designated offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more; and
-- src:10159 | (c) the victim of the designated offence is under the age of 18 years.
@ref s 490.012(1) (src:10156-10159)
-- "Subject to subsection (5), when a court imposes a sentence ... for a designated offence, it shall make an order in Form 52 ... if (a) prosecuted by indictment; (b) a term of imprisonment of two years or more;
-- and (c) the victim is under 18". The term is asked in months (24 months is two years: both ends of the threshold are tested).
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence on the person for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 490.011(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.012(5) the court may make an order in respect of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the designated offence was prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment imposed, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the age of the victim in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.012(1) the court shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court imposes a sentence on the person for the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT (`s 490.011(1) designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `s 490.012(5) the court may make an order in respect of the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court shall make an order under any of subsections (1) to (3) in respect of a secondary offence only if"
        IF `the designated offence was prosecuted by indictment` AND `the term of imprisonment imposed, in months` AT LEAST 24 AND `the age of the victim in years` LESS THAN 18 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the designated offence was prosecuted by indictment; (b) the sentence for the designated offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more; and (c) the victim of the designated offence is under the age of 18 years"

-- covers: 490.012(2), 490.012(2)(a), 490.012(2)(b)
-- jural: a person previously convicted of a primary offence or subject to an obligation > the court > liability
-- src:10161 | (2) Subject to subsection (5), when a court imposes a sentence on a person for a designated offence, it shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act if the prosecutor establishes that, before or after the coming into force of paragraphs (a) and (b), the person
-- src:10162 | (a) was previously convicted of a primary offence or previously convicted under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence; or
-- src:10163 | (b) is or was, as a result of a conviction, subject to an order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
@ref s 490.012(2) (src:10161-10163)
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence on the person for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 490.011(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.012(5) the court may make an order in respect of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor establishes that the person was previously convicted of a primary offence, or previously convicted under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor establishes that the person is or was, as a result of a conviction, subject to an order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.012(2) the court shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court imposes a sentence on the person for the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT (`s 490.011(1) designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `s 490.012(5) the court may make an order in respect of the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court shall make an order under any of subsections (1) to (3) in respect of a secondary offence only if"
        IF `the prosecutor establishes that the person was previously convicted of a primary offence, or previously convicted under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence` OR `the prosecutor establishes that the person is or was, as a result of a conviction, subject to an order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the prosecutor establishes that, before or after the coming into force of paragraphs (a) and (b), the person"

-- covers: 490.012(3), 490.012(3)(a), 490.012(3)(b)
-- fork: F12
-- jural: a person sentenced for, or found not criminally responsible for, a designated offence > the court > liability
-- src:10165 | (3) Subject to subsection (5), when a court imposes a sentence on a person for a designated offence in circumstances in which neither subsection (1) nor (2) applies, or when the court renders a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a designated offence, it shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act unless the court is satisfied the person has established that
-- src:10166 | (a) there would be no connection between making the order and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act; or
-- src:10167 | (b) the impact of the order on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act.
@ref s 490.012(3) (src:10165-10167)
-- "in circumstances in which neither subsection (1) nor (2) applies, or when the court renders a verdict of not criminally responsible ..., it shall make an order ... unless the court is satisfied the person has
-- established (a) ... or (b) ...". The answers of subsections (1) and (2) are inputs; a verdict of not criminally responsible is asked as a fact (fork F12: whether (1) or (2) applying defeats (3) for such a verdict).
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence on the person for the offence, or renders a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court renders a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 490.011(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.012(5) the court may make an order in respect of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.012(1) the court shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 490.012(2) the court shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there would be no connection between making the order and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the order on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.012(3) the court shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court imposes a sentence on the person for the offence, or renders a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for it` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT (`s 490.011(1) designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `s 490.012(5) the court may make an order in respect of the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court shall make an order under any of subsections (1) to (3) in respect of a secondary offence only if"
        IF (NOT `the court renders a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`) AND (`s 490.012(1) the court shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 490.012(2) the court shall make an order in Form 52 requiring the person to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in circumstances in which neither subsection (1) nor (2) applies"
        IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there would be no connection between making the order and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders` OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the order on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is satisfied the person has established that"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 490.012(4) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.012(4)(a) the nature and seriousness of the designated offence`
    `s 490.012(4)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics`
    `s 490.012(4)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim`
    `s 490.012(4)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person`
    `s 490.012(4)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence`
    `s 490.012(4)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person`
    `s 490.012(4)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant`

-- covers: 490.012(4), 490.012(4)(a), 490.012(4)(b), 490.012(4)(c), 490.012(4)(d), 490.012(4)(e), 490.012(4)(f), 490.012(4)(g)
-- jural: the person concerned > the court > right
-- src:10169 | (4) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (3) in respect of a person, the court shall consider
-- src:10170 | (a) the nature and seriousness of the designated offence;
-- src:10171 | (b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics;
-- src:10172 | (c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim;
-- src:10173 | (d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person;
-- src:10174 | (e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence;
-- src:10175 | (f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person; and
-- src:10176 | (g) any other factors that the court considers relevant.
@ref s 490.012(4) (src:10169-10176)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 490.012(4) factor`
      `the court considers the other factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.012(4) the court shall consider the factor in determining whether to make an order under subsection (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF factor EQUALS `s 490.012(4)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` AND NOT `the court considers the other factor relevant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 490.013 -- Duration of order`

DECLARE `s 490.013 duration` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.013(2)(a) the order ends 10 years after it was made`
    `s 490.013(2)(b) the order ends 20 years after it was made`
    `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life`

DECLARE `s 490.013 facts of an offence` HAS
    `it was prosecuted summarily`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maximum term of imprisonment in years`    IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum term of imprisonment is life`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- covers: 490.013(1)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the court > liability
-- src:10180 | 490.013 (1) An order made under section 490.012 begins on the day on which it is made.
@ref s 490.013(1) (src:10180)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 490.013(1) the day on which the order begins` MEANS `the day on which the order is made`

-- covers: 490.013(2), 490.013(2)(a), 490.013(2)(b), 490.013(2)(c)
-- fork: F13
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the court > liability
-- src:10182 | (2) An order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3)
-- src:10183 | (a) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 10 years after it was made if the offence in connection with which it was made was prosecuted summarily or if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years;
-- src:10184 | (b) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 20 years after it was made if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years; and
-- src:10185 | (c) applies for life if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is life.
@ref s 490.013(2) (src:10182-10185)
-- Subject to (3) and (5). (a) ends 10 years after it was made if the offence was prosecuted summarily or the maximum term of imprisonment is two or five years; (b) ends 20 years after if the maximum is 10 or 14 years;
-- (c) applies for life if the maximum is life. A maximum of any other number of years: the text is silent (NOTHING; fork F13).
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 490.013 facts of an offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.013 duration`
`s 490.013(2) the duration of an order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3) apart from subsections (3) and (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offence`'s `the maximum term of imprisonment is life` THEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life`
        IF `the offence`'s `it was prosecuted summarily` THEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(a) the order ends 10 years after it was made`
        IF `the offence`'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in years` EQUALS 2 OR `the offence`'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in years` EQUALS 5 THEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(a) the order ends 10 years after it was made`
        IF `the offence`'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in years` EQUALS 10 OR `the offence`'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in years` EQUALS 14 THEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(b) the order ends 20 years after it was made`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- covers: 490.013(3), 490.013(3)(a), 490.013(3)(b)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the court > liability
-- src:10188 | (3) An order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3) applies for life if
-- src:10189 | (a) in the same proceeding, the person has been convicted of, or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered for, two or more designated offences in connection with which an order under any of subsections 490.012(1) to (3) may be made; and
-- src:10190 | (b) the court is satisfied that those offences demonstrate, or form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature.
@ref s 490.013(3) (src:10188-10190)
GIVEN `in the same proceeding the person has been convicted of, or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered for, two or more designated offences in connection with which an order under any of subsections 490.012(1) to (3) may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that those offences demonstrate, or form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.013(3) an order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3) applies for life` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `in the same proceeding the person has been convicted of, or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered for, two or more designated offences in connection with which an order under any of subsections 490.012(1) to (3) may be made` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the court is satisfied that those offences demonstrate, or form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies for life if (a) in the same proceeding, the person has been convicted of"

-- covers: 490.013(4)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the court > liability
-- src:10192 | (4) If paragraph (3)(a) applies in the circumstances but the court is not satisfied as set out in paragraph (3)(b), the duration of the order is determined by applying paragraphs (2)(a) to (c) to the designated offence with the longest maximum term of imprisonment.
@ref s 490.013(4) (src:10192)
GIVEN `paragraph (3)(a) applies in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied as set out in paragraph (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
