DECLARE `s 490.013 the subsection of section 490.012 under which the order was made` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.013 subsection 490.012(1)`
    `s 490.013 subsection 490.012(2)`
    `s 490.013 subsection 490.012(3)`

-- The duration of an order, with subsections (2) to (6) put together: (6) an order under 490.012(2) is for life; for an order under (1) or (3): (5) for life; (3) for life when (a) and (b); (4) when (a) only,
-- (2) applied to the offence with the longest maximum term; otherwise (2).
-- src:10182 | (2) An order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3)
-- src:10183 | (a) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 10 years after it was made if the offence in connection with which it was made was prosecuted summarily or if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years;
-- src:10184 | (b) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 20 years after it was made if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years; and
-- src:10185 | (c) applies for life if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is life.
-- src:10186 | (2.1) [Repealed, 2023, c. 28, s. 8]
-- src:10187 | Duration of order — offences in same proceeding
-- src:10188 | (3) An order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3) applies for life if
-- src:10189 | (a) in the same proceeding, the person has been convicted of, or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder is rendered for, two or more designated offences in connection with which an order under any of subsections 490.012(1) to (3) may be made; and
-- src:10190 | (b) the court is satisfied that those offences demonstrate, or form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature.
-- src:10191 | If court not satisfied
-- src:10192 | (4) If paragraph (3)(a) applies in the circumstances but the court is not satisfied as set out in paragraph (3)(b), the duration of the order is determined by applying paragraphs (2)(a) to (c) to the designated offence with the longest maximum term of imprisonment.
-- src:10193 | Duration of order — other order or obligation
-- src:10194 | (5) An order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3) applies for life if the person
-- src:10195 | (a) was previously convicted of, or previously received a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, a primary offence or an offence under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence; or
-- src:10196 | (b) is, or was at any time, the subject of an order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
-- src:10197 | Duration of order — s. 490.012(2)
-- src:10198 | (6) An order made under subsection 490.012(2) applies for life.
@ref s 490.013(2) to (6) together (src:10182-10198)
GIVEN `how the order was made` IS A `s 490.013 the subsection of section 490.012 under which the order was made`
      `the offence` IS A `s 490.013 facts of an offence`
      `the designated offence with the longest maximum term of imprisonment` IS A `s 490.013 facts of an offence`
      `paragraph (3)(a) applies in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied as set out in paragraph (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.013 duration`
`s 490.013 the duration of the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how the order was made` EQUALS `s 490.013 subsection 490.012(2)` THEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life`
        IF `subsection (5) applies` THEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life`
        IF `paragraph (3)(a) applies in the circumstances` AND `the court is satisfied as set out in paragraph (3)(b)` THEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life`
        IF `paragraph (3)(a) applies in the circumstances` THEN `s 490.013(4) the duration of the order when the court is not satisfied as set out in paragraph (3)(b)` `paragraph (3)(a) applies in the circumstances` `the court is satisfied as set out in paragraph (3)(b)` `the designated offence with the longest maximum term of imprisonment`
        OTHERWISE `s 490.013(2) the duration of an order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3) apart from subsections (3) and (5)` `the offence`

-- The day the order ends: 10 or 20 years after the day it was made (fork F5: the text has no rule for counting the day); a life order has no end.
-- fork: F5
-- src:10183 | (a) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 10 years after it was made if the offence in connection with which it was made was prosecuted summarily or if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years;
-- src:10184 | (b) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 20 years after it was made if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years; and
-- src:10185 | (c) applies for life if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is life.
@ref s 490.013(2) (the day the order ends) (src:10183-10185)
GIVEN `the day on which the order was made` IS A DATE
      duration IS A `s 490.013 duration`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 490.013(2) the day on which the order ends` MEANS
    CONSIDER duration
    WHEN `s 490.013(2)(a) the order ends 10 years after it was made` THEN JUST (`add years` `the day on which the order was made` 10)
    WHEN `s 490.013(2)(b) the order ends 20 years after it was made` THEN JUST (`add years` `the day on which the order was made` 20)
    WHEN `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

DECLARE `s 490.0131 decision` IS ONE OF
