§ `Section 490.014 -- Appeal`

DECLARE `s 490.014 appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.014 the prosecutor`
    `s 490.014 a person who is subject to an order made under section 490.012`
    `s 490.014 someone else`

DECLARE `s 490.014 ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.014 a question of law`
    `s 490.014 a question of mixed law and fact`
    `s 490.014 another ground`

-- covers: 490.014
-- jural: the prosecutor or a person subject to an order > the appeal court > power
-- src:10210 | 490.014 The prosecutor, or a person who is subject to an order made under section 490.012, may appeal from a decision of the court under section 490.012 or 490.013 on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may
@ref s 490.014 (src:10210)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.014 appellant`
      `the decision is a decision of the court under section 490.012 or 490.013` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 490.014 ground of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.014 the person may appeal from the decision of the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.014 someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the decision is a decision of the court under section 490.012 or 490.013` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF ground EQUALS `s 490.014 another ground` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 490.014 disposition of the appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.014(a) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.014(b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.014(b) allow the appeal and quash the order`
    `s 490.014(b) allow the appeal and amend the order`
    `s 490.014(b) allow the appeal and make an order that may be made under section 490.012`
    `s 490.014 another disposition`

-- covers: 490.014(a), 490.014(b)
-- jural: the prosecutor or a person subject to an order > the appeal court > power
-- src:10211 | (a) dismiss the appeal; or
-- src:10212 | (b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the order or make an order that may be made under section 490.012.
@ref s 490.014(a) and (b) (src:10211-10212)
GIVEN disposition IS A `s 490.014 disposition of the appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.014 the appeal court may make the disposition` MEANS
