    WHEN `s 490.014 another disposition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 490.015 -- Application for termination order`

DECLARE `s 490.015(1) kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.015(1)(a) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(a)`
    `s 490.015(1)(b) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(b)`
    `s 490.015(1)(c) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(c) or in any of subsections 490.013(3), (5) or (6)`
    `s 490.015(1) another order`

-- covers: 490.015(1), 490.015(1)(a), 490.015(1)(b), 490.015(1)(c)
-- fork: F10,F5
-- jural: a person subject to an order > the court > power
-- src:10214 | 490.015 (1) A person who is subject to an order may apply for a termination order
-- src:10215 | (a) if five years have elapsed since the order was made, in the case of an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(a);
-- src:10216 | (b) if 10 years have elapsed since the order was made, in the case of an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(b); or
-- src:10217 | (c) if 20 years have elapsed since the order was made, in the case of an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(c) or in any of subsections 490.013(3), (5) or (6).
@ref s 490.015(1) (src:10214-10217)
-- "A person who is subject to an order may apply for a termination order (a) if five years have elapsed since the order was made ...; (b) if 10 years ...; (c) if 20 years ...": a grant gated by "if" and by a period.
-- Answered NOTHING before the period has run (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1)); the other reading is JUST FALSE (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): fork F10.
GIVEN `kind of order` IS A `s 490.015(1) kind of order`
      `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.015(1) the person may apply for a termination order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `kind of order` EQUALS `s 490.015(1) another order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `kind of order` EQUALS `s 490.015(1)(a) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(a)` AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `add years` `the day the order was made` 5 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `kind of order` EQUALS `s 490.015(1)(b) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(b)` AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `add years` `the day the order was made` 10 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `kind of order` EQUALS `s 490.015(1)(c) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(c) or in any of subsections 490.013(3), (5) or (6)` AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `add years` `the day the order was made` 20 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

@ref s 490.015(1) (the earliest day) (src:10214-10217)
GIVEN `kind of order` IS A `s 490.015(1) kind of order`
      `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 490.015(1) the earliest day on which the person may apply for a termination order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `kind of order`
    WHEN `s 490.015(1)(a) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(a)` THEN JUST (`add years` `the day the order was made` 5)
    WHEN `s 490.015(1)(b) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(b)` THEN JUST (`add years` `the day the order was made` 10)
    WHEN `s 490.015(1)(c) an order referred to in paragraph 490.013(2)(c) or in any of subsections 490.013(3), (5) or (6)` THEN JUST (`add years` `the day the order was made` 20)
    WHEN `s 490.015(1) another order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 490.015(2)
-- fork: F10,F5
-- jural: a person subject to more than one order > the court > power
