-- src:10225 | (5) A person whose application is refused may re-apply if five years have elapsed since they made the previous application. They may also re-apply once they receive a pardon or once a record suspension is ordered. However, they may not re-apply under this subsection if an order is made with respect to them under section 490.012 of this Act or section 227.01 of the National Defence Act after the previous application was made.
@ref s 490.015(5) (src:10225)
-- "A person whose application is refused may re-apply if five years have elapsed since they made the previous application. They may also re-apply once they receive a pardon or once a record suspension is ordered.
-- However, they may not re-apply under this subsection if an order is made ... after the previous application was made.": the last sentence is a flat negative (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `the person’s application was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person made the previous application` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the person receives a pardon or a record suspension is ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made with respect to the person under section 490.012 of this Act or section 227.01 of the National Defence Act after the previous application was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.015(5) the person may re-apply for a termination order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person’s application was refused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `an order is made with respect to the person under section 490.012 of this Act or section 227.01 of the National Defence Act after the previous application was made` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they may not re-apply under this subsection if an order is made with respect to them under section 490.012 of this Act or section 227.01 of the National Defence Act after the previous application was made"
        IF `the day in question` AT LEAST `add years` `the day the person made the previous application` 5 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person receives a pardon or a record suspension is ordered` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

DECLARE `s 490.015(6) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.015(6)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 490.015(6)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`

-- covers: 490.015(6), 490.015(6)(a), 490.015(6)(b)
-- jural: a person subject to an order > the court > power
