-- src:10228 | (a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction if
-- src:10229 | (i) one or more of the orders to which it relates were made by such a court under section 490.012, or
-- src:10230 | (ii) one or more of the orders to which it relates were made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.03(6) of that Act; or
-- src:10231 | (b) a court of criminal jurisdiction, in any other case in which the application relates to one or more orders made under section 490.012.
@ref s 490.015(6) (src:10227-10231)
GIVEN `one or more of the orders to which the application relates were made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction under section 490.012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more of the orders were made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.03(6) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application relates to one or more orders made under section 490.012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.015(6) court`
`s 490.015(6) the court to which the application shall be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one or more of the orders to which the application relates were made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction under section 490.012` OR `one or more of the orders were made under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.03(6) of that Act` THEN JUST `s 490.015(6)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
        IF `the application relates to one or more orders made under section 490.012` THEN JUST `s 490.015(6)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§ `Section 490.016 -- Termination order`

-- covers: 490.016(1), 490.016(1)(a), 490.016(1)(b)
-- jural: a person subject to an order > the court > right
