§ `Section 490.017 -- Appeal of termination order decision`

DECLARE `s 490.017 appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.017 the prosecutor`
    `s 490.017 the person who applied for a termination order`
    `s 490.017 someone else`

-- covers: 490.017(1)
-- jural: the prosecutor or the person who applied > the appeal court > power
-- src:10250 | 490.017 (1) The prosecutor or the person who applied for a termination order may appeal from a decision made under subsection 490.016(1) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, or allow it and order a new hearing, quash the termination order or make an order that may be made under that subsection.
@ref s 490.017(1) (src:10250)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.017 appellant`
      `the decision is a decision made under subsection 490.016(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 490.014 ground of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.017(1) the person may appeal from the decision made under subsection 490.016(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.017 someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the decision is a decision made under subsection 490.016(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF ground EQUALS `s 490.014 another ground` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 490.017 disposition of the appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.017(1) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.017(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.017(1) allow the appeal and quash the termination order`
    `s 490.017(1) allow the appeal and make an order that may be made under subsection 490.016(1)`
    `s 490.017 another disposition`

