§ `Section 490.018 -- Requirements relating to notice`

DECLARE `s 490.018(1) thing the court shall cause` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.018(1)(a) the order to be read by or to the person who is subject to it`
    `s 490.018(1)(b) a copy of the order to be given to that person`
    `s 490.018(1)(c) that person to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act`
    `s 490.018(1)(d)(i) a copy of the order to be sent to the Review Board that is responsible for making a disposition with respect to that person`
    `s 490.018(1)(d)(ii) a copy of the order to be sent to the person in charge of the place in which that person is to serve the custodial portion of a sentence or is to be detained in custody as part of a disposition under Part XX.1`
    `s 490.018(1)(d)(iii) a copy of the order to be sent to the police service whose member charged that person with the offence in connection with which the order is made`
    `s 490.018(1)(d)(iv) a copy of the order to be sent to the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and, if there is a responsible provincial police service, the head of that police service`

-- covers: 490.018(1), 490.018(1)(a), 490.018(1)(b), 490.018(1)(c), 490.018(1)(d)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the court or appeal court > right
-- src:10254 | 490.018 (1) When a court or appeal court makes an order under section 490.012, it shall cause
-- src:10255 | (a) the order to be read by or to the person who is subject to it;
-- src:10256 | (b) a copy of the order to be given to that person;
-- src:10257 | (c) that person to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act; and
-- src:10258 | (d) a copy of the order to be sent to
-- src:10259 | (i) the Review Board that is responsible for making a disposition with respect to that person, if applicable,
-- src:10260 | (ii) the person in charge of the place in which that person is to serve the custodial portion of a sentence or is to be detained in custody as part of a disposition under Part XX.1, if applicable,
-- src:10261 | (iii) the police service whose member charged that person with the offence in connection with which the order is made, and
-- src:10262 | (iv) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and, if there is a provincial police service that is responsible for the registration of information under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act in the province in which the court makes the order, the head of that police service.
@ref s 490.018(1) (src:10254-10262)
-- Items (d)(i) and (d)(ii) are "if applicable": JUST FALSE when the item does not apply.
GIVEN `a court or appeal court makes an order under section 490.012` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `s 490.018(1) thing the court shall cause`
      `the item is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.018(1) the court shall cause the thing to be done` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court or appeal court makes an order under section 490.012` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF thing EQUALS `s 490.018(1)(d)(i) a copy of the order to be sent to the Review Board that is responsible for making a disposition with respect to that person` AND NOT `the item is applicable` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Review Board that is responsible for making a disposition with respect to that person, if applicable"
        IF thing EQUALS `s 490.018(1)(d)(ii) a copy of the order to be sent to the person in charge of the place in which that person is to serve the custodial portion of a sentence or is to be detained in custody as part of a disposition under Part XX.1` AND NOT `the item is applicable` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or is to be detained in custody as part of a disposition under Part XX.1, if applicable"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 490.018(2)
-- jural: the court > the person subject to the order > right
-- src:10264 | (2) After paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) have been complied with, the person who is subject to the order shall endorse the order.
@ref s 490.018(2) (src:10264)
GIVEN `paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.018(2) the person who is subject to the order shall endorse the order` MEANS
    IF `paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) have been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) have been complied with"

DECLARE `s 490.018(3) direction of the Review Board` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.018(3)(a) that the person be discharged absolutely under paragraph 672.54(a)`
    `s 490.018(3)(b) that the person be discharged subject to conditions under paragraph 672.54(b)`
    `s 490.018(3) another direction`

-- covers: 490.018(3), 490.018(3)(a), 490.018(3)(b)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > a Review Board > right
-- src:10266 | (3) A Review Board shall cause a copy of the order to be given to the person who is subject to it when it directs
-- src:10267 | (a) under paragraph 672.54(a), that the person be discharged absolutely; or
-- src:10268 | (b) under paragraph 672.54(b), that the person be discharged subject to conditions, unless the conditions restrict the person’s liberty in a manner and to an extent that prevent them from complying with sections 4, 4.1, 4.3 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
@ref s 490.018(3) (src:10266-10268)
GIVEN direction IS A `s 490.018(3) direction of the Review Board`
      `the conditions restrict the person’s liberty in a manner and to an extent that prevent them from complying with sections 4, 4.1, 4.3 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.018(3) the Review Board shall cause a copy of the order to be given to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF direction EQUALS `s 490.018(3) another direction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF direction EQUALS `s 490.018(3)(a) that the person be discharged absolutely under paragraph 672.54(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the conditions restrict the person’s liberty in a manner and to an extent that prevent them from complying with sections 4, 4.1, 4.3 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the conditions restrict the person’s liberty in a manner and to an extent that prevent them from complying with sections 4, 4.1, 4.3 and 6 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 490.018(4)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the person in charge of the place of custody > right
-- src:10270 | (4) The person in charge of the place in which the person is serving the custodial portion of a sentence, or is detained in custody, before their release or discharge shall give the person a copy of the order not earlier than 10 days before their release or discharge.
@ref s 490.018(4) (src:10270)
-- The person in charge shall give the person a copy "not earlier than 10 days before their release or discharge": the earliest day is the day of release or discharge less ten days.
GIVEN `the day of the release or discharge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 490.018(4) the earliest day on which the person in charge shall give the person a copy of the order` MEANS
    `the day of the release or discharge` MINUS 10

GIVEN `the day of the release or discharge` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.018(4) the person in charge shall give the person a copy of the order on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 490.018(4) the earliest day on which the person in charge shall give the person a copy of the order` `the day of the release or discharge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not earlier than 10 days before their release or discharge"
        IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the day of the release or discharge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before their release or discharge shall give the person a copy of the order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 490.019 -- Obligation to comply (convictions before December 15, 2004)`

-- covers: 490.019
-- jural: the Attorney General or minister of justice > a person served with a notice in Form 53 > power
-- src:10274 | 490.019 A person who is served with a notice in Form 53 shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for the applicable period specified in section 490.022 unless a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.023(2).
@ref s 490.019 (src:10274)
-- "A person who is served with a notice in Form 53 shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for the applicable period specified in section 490.022 unless a court makes an exemption order
-- under subsection 490.023(2)." The period (section 490.022) and the exemption order (section 490.023) belong to another part: seam inputs. Not served: NOTHING (limited by its own wording).
GIVEN `the person is served with a notice in Form 53` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 490.022 the person is within the applicable period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.023(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.019 the person shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is served with a notice in Form 53` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.023(2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.023(2)"
        IF `s 490.022 the person is within the applicable period` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the applicable period specified in section 490.022"
        IF `s 490.022 the person is within the applicable period` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

§ `The seam out: is an order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act in force`

-- ccc18 (sections 490.02 to 490.027 and 490.04) asks this by name. An order made under section 490.012 begins on the day it is made (490.013(1)) and runs for the duration of 490.013 (10 or 20 years after it was
-- made, or for life). A termination order is named in section 490.016 but its effect on the order is not stated in these sources (NOTHING).
-- src:10180 | 490.013 (1) An order made under section 490.012 begins on the day on which it is made.
-- src:10181 | Duration of order — s. 490.012(1) or (3)
-- src:10182 | (2) An order made under subsection 490.012(1) or (3)
-- src:10183 | (a) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 10 years after it was made if the offence in connection with which it was made was prosecuted summarily or if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years;
-- src:10184 | (b) subject to subsections (3) and (5), ends 20 years after it was made if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years; and
-- src:10185 | (c) applies for life if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is life.
@ref seam out (an order is in force) (src:10180-10185)
GIVEN `an order was made under section 490.012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `s 490.013 the duration of the order` IS A MAYBE `s 490.013 duration`
      `a termination order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.012 an order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act is in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order was made under section 490.012` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 490.013(1) the day on which the order begins` `the day on which the order was made` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under section 490.012 begins on the day on which it is made."
        IF `a termination order has been made` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `s 490.013 the duration of the order`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
                  WHEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(c) the order applies for life` THEN JUST TRUE
                  WHEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(a) the order ends 10 years after it was made` THEN IF `the day in question` AT MOST (`add years` `the day on which the order was made` 10) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ends 10 years after it was made if the offence in connection with which it was made was prosecuted summarily"
                  WHEN JUST `s 490.013(2)(b) the order ends 20 years after it was made` THEN IF `the day in question` AT MOST (`add years` `the day on which the order was made` 20) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ends 20 years after it was made if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years"
